<title>UK: EU grants free market barley.</title>
<headline>EU grants free market barley.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following licences to export free market grain to non-EU countries, member-country officials said.</p>
<p>		  Tonnage	  Maximum rebate</p>
<p>Barley	   21,450	  14.00  ECU/tonne</p>
<p>Bids for open market rye, oats for Switzerland and Liechtenstein and Finnish intervention barley were rejected, they said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
